.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/victory-vendor Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "VictoryVendor"
.PP
Vendored dependencies for Victory\&.
.SH "Background"
.PP
D3 has released most of its libraries as ESM-only\&. This means that consumers in Node\&.js applications can no longer just \fRrequire()\fP anything with a d3 transitive dependency, including much of Victory\&.

.PP
To help provide an easy path to folks still using CommonJS in their Node\&.js applications that consume Victory, we now provide this package to vendor in various d3-related packages\&.
.SH "Packages"
.PP
We presently provide the following top-level libraries:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-ease
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-interpolate
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-scale
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-shape
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-timer
.PP

.PP
This is the total list of top and transitive libraries we vendor:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-array
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-color
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-ease
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-format
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-interpolate
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-path
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-scale
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-shape
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-time
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-time-format
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-timer
.IP "\(bu" 2
internmap
.PP

.PP
Note that this does \fInot\fP include the following D3 libraries that still support CommonJS:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
d3-voronoi
.PP
.SH "How it works"
.PP
We provide two alternate paths and behaviors -- for ESM and CommonJS
.SS "ESM"
If you do a Node\&.js import like:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { interpolate } from "victory\-vendor/d3\-interpolate";
.fi
.PP

.PP
under the hood it's going to just re-export and pass you through to \fRnode_modules/d3-interpolate\fP, the \fBreal\fP ESM library from D3\&.
.SS "CommonJS"
If you do a Node\&.js import like:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const { interpolate } = require("victory\-vendor/d3\-interpolate");
.fi
.PP

.PP
under the hood it's going to will go to an alternate path that contains the transpiled version of the underlying d3 library to be found at \fRvictory-vendor/lib-vendor/d3-interpolate/**/*\&.js\fP\&. This futher has internally consistent import references to other \fRvictory-vendor/lib-vendor/<pkg-name>\fP paths\&.

.PP
Note that for some tooling (like Jest) that doesn't play well with \fRpackage\&.json:exports\fP routing to this CommonJS path, we \fBalso\fP output a root file in the form of \fRvictory-vendor/d3-interpolate\&.js\fP\&.
